 r←Test_Log_104(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;tempDir;msg;rc;L;lines;filename;list;expected
⍝ Usage data files that are not needed any more are deleted, CSV and ZIP alike: files up to a
⍝ month of a year that has a file for the whole year, and files up to a month that a later one of
⍝ the same year supersedes. Files for whole years and the backups of the log file stay.
⍝ This is what production looked like: sporadic monthly files of years that are long finished.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 r←T._Failed

 tempDir←∆GetTempDir'-Log/'
 rc←'Create!'F.CheckPath tempDir
 Assert rc
 L←##.Server.Logs
 lines←⊃F.NGET(∆TEMP_TEST_DATA,'/LogFile/app-log.txt')1
 lines←('2024-'∘≡¨5↑¨lines)/lines                   ⍝ Only the data of the current year: Jan to Mar 2024
 (⊂lines)F.NPUT(tempDir,L.GetLogFilename)1
 :For filename :In ,'usage-data-2023' 'usage-data-2023-05' 'usage-data-2023-11' 'usage-data-2024-01'∘.,'.csv' '.zip'
     (⊂'Group,Name,Version,Year,Month,Downloads')F.NPUT(tempDir,filename)1
 :EndFor
 (⊂'Backup')F.NPUT(tempDir,'app-log-2023.bkp.zip')1
 L.ProcessLogFile tempDir(2024 3 4)

 list←{⊃,/1↓⎕NPARTS ⍵}¨F.ListFiles tempDir,'*'
 expected←'app-log-2023.bkp.zip' 'app-log.txt' 'usage-data-2023.csv' 'usage-data-2023.zip' 'usage-data-2024-02.csv' 'usage-data-2024-02.zip'
 →T.GoToTidyUp~list ∆LazyMatch expected

 r←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 (rc msg)←F.RmDirByForce tempDir
 msg Assert rc=0
⍝Done
